# OpenRouter Integration

This project has been modified to use [OpenRouter](https://openrouter.ai/) as a unified API for accessing multiple LLM providers. Instead of using separate API keys for OpenAI and Google Gemini, you can now use a single OpenRouter API key to access both models.

## Model Mapping

The following models are used through OpenRouter:

| Original Model | OpenRouter Equivalent |
|---------------|----------------------|
| gemini-2.0-flash | google/gemini-flash-1.5 |
| gpt-4.1 | openai/gpt-4o |
| gpt-4.1-mini | openai/gpt-4o-mini |

## Setup

1. Sign up for an account at [OpenRouter](https://openrouter.ai/)
2. Create an API key in your OpenRouter dashboard
3. Add your OpenRouter API key to the `.env` file:

```env
TAVILY_API_KEY=your_tavily_key
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_key
```

## Benefits

- **Single API Key**: Manage just one API key instead of multiple provider keys
- **Model Flexibility**: Easily switch between different models from various providers
- **Cost Management**: OpenRouter provides transparent pricing and usage tracking
- **Fallback Options**: If one provider is unavailable, OpenRouter can route to alternatives

For more information about OpenRouter, visit their [documentation](https://openrouter.ai/docs).
